# =============================================================================
# .gitignore -- 2D-DWE
#
# WHAT BELONGS IN THE REPO
#   Source, the .pro, the design and readme, the case INPUTS (cases/c6/), and
#   the tools that regenerate everything else. That set is enough to reproduce
#   any result from scratch.
#
# WHAT DOES NOT
#   Run output. It is large and it is derived: the current run directories hold
#   ~1.1 GB, of which out_c6_3m alone is 879 MB. A single .vti frame at 3 m is
#   ~60 MB of ASCII. Git stores every version of every one of those forever, so
#   one careless `git add -A` permanently inflates the history even if the files
#   are deleted in the next commit.
#
# To commit a specific figure anyway, override deliberately:
#     git add -f docs/some_figure.png
# =============================================================================

# --- build artefacts (qmake) -------------------------------------------------
Makefile
Makefile.qmake
build/
bin/
*.pro.user
*.pro.user.*

# object files, libraries, executables
*.d
*.o
*.obj
*.slo
*.lo
*.gch
*.pch
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.a
*.la
*.lai
*.lib
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.mod
*.smod

# --- run output --------------------------------------------------------------
# Directories: every case writes to out_<name>/ or whatever --out is given.
out/
out_*/

# Run logs. The previous rule only caught DIRECTORIES, so out_c6_3m.log and
# out_c6_10m_tr.log slipped through and were committed as tracked files.
*.log

# Result formats, wherever they land -- these are always derived.
*.vti
*.vtp
*.vtu
*.vtr
*.pvd
*.pvti
*.tif
*.tiff
*.npy

# Figures are regenerated by tools/plot_c6.py. Force-add if one is needed
# as documentation (see the header).
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.pdf

# --- inputs that are NOT ours to redistribute --------------------------------
# Terrain and land cover live in the GIS project and are referenced by path, not
# copied here. If one is ever staged locally, keep it out of the history: the
# C6 DEM alone is 4372 x 2106 at 1 m.
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.qix
*.cpg
*.dss

# --- python tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- explicit keeps ----------------------------------------------------------
# Case inputs are small, are parameters rather than results, and are what makes
# a run reproducible. Re-include them after the broad rules above.
!cases/**/*.csv
!cases/**/*.txt
!cases/**/*.json
